              ('ctx', 'However, sometimes we do things that appear to be morally wrong but, in fact, are not. If we are reproached, we can give an explanation for our action that justifies it. In these cases, we are claiming that, despite appearances to the contrary, what we did was morally permissible.'),
              ('conc', 'Forgiveness and justification ought to be distinguished.'),
